Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:39:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 064/154] feat: tear off a sidebar tab into a little window,
 route cross-window sidebar drops
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MoveWebContentsBetweenStrips and AdoptTabIntoLittleWindow give
a tab a live, no-reload path out of its current strip into a fresh little
window. sidebar-drag.js/sidebar.js now report a drag's release point when it
resolves to no drop kind of its own, which
ClassifyAndRouteDroppedTab classifies against every other live Atrium
window and RouteSidebarDrop acts
on for the same-workspace case.
MoveLittleTabToSpace and the IsLittle() close-suppression gate finish
the foyer's "move to space" button, using the same tear-off
primitive and a small extracted decision (atrium_move_target_decision) for
which resident window it lands on.

The accompanying browsertest suite (wired as one browser_tests source_set
in BUILD.gn) covers the tear-off, drop-routing, and
multi-window teardown paths, including the specific second-profile-window
close-before-teardown fix isolated for a VM crash in
BrowserCompositorMac.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
